      "content": "it just feels so much more real than a \"hallucination.\" like, the heat signatures follow the movement of the cat perfectly, they aren't just random shapes. and when the humming changes pitch, it's exactly when the lights flicker or the appliance turns on. it's too consistent for it to be just my brain making things up. \n\nif we set aside the medical possibility for a second and just look at the concept of human potential—if a person's sensory threshold actually *did* expand like this, what kind of physiological adaptations would be necessary to handle that much data? like, how would the brain actually integrate this new input?",
